<title>USA: Jayhawk Q4 net loss $0.33 vs profit.</title>
<headline>Jayhawk Q4 net loss $0.33 vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.33   profit	 $0.09</p>
<p> Net loss		   7,940   profit	 1,794</p>
<p> Revs			16,174		    7,545</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	24,270		   20,800</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.00		    $0.26</p>
<p> Net			     91		    4,900</p>
<p> Revs			53,566		   21,788</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	23,274		   18,732</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Q4 net loss is attributable to a special charge of $15.5 million taken to increase the allowance for credit losses.  </p>
<p>The special charge resulted from the company's reevaluation of the recoverability of advances made to certain of its participating dealers.</p>
<p>As a result of the reevaluation, the company terminated its relationship with certain dealers and changed the basis upon which the company is willing to purchase installment contracts with others.</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Jayhawk Acceptance Corp.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
